st present a GRE score of 1000 or higher (verbal + quantitative)\n-must show evidence of an active research history\nRegular Teaching Assistantship: - $16,500/year\nRequirements:\n-must receive regular admission status\n-must present a GPA of 3.4 in one of the following disciplines: Chemistry or Biology\n(laboratory and/or lecture).\n-must present a valid GRE score\n-must present a transcript indicative of teaching ability\nACE Implementation Research Stipend - $25,000/year\nRequirements:\n-Open only to junior or senior Doctoral Students\n-must be a citizen or permanent resident of the United States of America\n-must present a GPA of 3.0 on the 4.0 scale\n-must present a GRE score of 1000\n-should contact Dr. John Owens at 225-771-3750 or jowens8960@aol.com\nFor Application Click here:\nEducational Loans/Work Study Program - Variable\nRequirements:\n-Please contact the Financial Aid Office, Southern University, as soon as possible for information about these programs (225-771-2790 or at www.subr.edu).\nRELATED INFO\nEnvironmental Toxicology HomePage\nDirector's Message\nAdmission Requirements\nFaculty and Staff\nFinancial Assistance\nGraduate Curriculum\nStudent Research Education Enhancement Program\nAnnouncements\nSouthern University and A&M College\n801 Harding Blvd\nBaton Rouge, LA 70807\n(225) 771-4500\nStaff Directory\nAdministration\nMission & Vision\nCareers\nStudent Code of Conduct & Policies\nTitle IX\nNotice of Nondiscrimination\nUniformed Policy on Campus Free Speech\nSACSCOC Accreditation\nAccessibility Statement\nCustomer Service Survey\nHEERF I-CARES Act, II-CRRSAA and III-ARP\nHEERF I-CARES Act\nHEERF II-CRRSAA\nHEERF III-ARP-CRRSAA\nHurricane Preparedness\nA Member of the\nSOUTHERN UNIVERSITY SYSTEM\nSU Baton Rouge\nSU New Orleans\nSU Shreveport\nSU Law Center\nSU AG Center", "links": [["Privacy Statement", "http://www.sus.edu/page/su-privacy-statement"], ["", "https://www.facebook.com/southernuniversitybatonrouge/"], ["", "https://twitter.com/South